1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:10,475
If a website shows what users type without care, an attacker can type code instead of a name, and it runs in other people's browsers.

2
00:00:11,170 --> 00:00:16,795
It is like a notice board where someone pins a trap instead of a notice.

3
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:26,800
A comment box shows names. An attacker types a script instead of a name. Every visitor's browser now runs it.

4
00:00:27,500 --> 00:00:33,750
Display it as text, and the browser shows harmless characters instead of running code.

5
00:00:35,450 --> 00:00:44,450
Treat user text as text, never as code. Use text content, not inner HTML, and escape special characters.

6
00:00:45,150 --> 00:00:51,575
A content security policy adds a second wall, blocking scripts you did not allow.

